 * Written by a test run on that tag, not by hand. Lanes `a` (weight 1), `b` (`1/3`) and `c` (1)
 * under `golden`, booted whole, one unit a lease, each completed at cost 1: three picks with all
 * three waiting, then six with `c` idle. Then the root's origin is raised to 3 units, a value a
 * rebase over those three could reach, whole on each of their grids. Lane `d` (`1/5`) is applied
 * at generation 2, and two picks with all four waiting seat `d` under that origin, where `3 · 16 / 5`
 * is not whole, and clamp `c`, leaving it a wake offset of 72 ticks. Lane `e` (1) is applied at
 * generation 3 and never picked, so its edge has no gauge. `c` stands below the origin. A 0.7.5
